<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kagera Salient</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kagera Salient is a strip of Tanzanian territory north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kagera-river">Kagera River</a>, west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-victoria">Lake Victoria</a> and bordering Uganda. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/idi-amin">Idi Amin</a>'s Ugandan army invaded and annexed it in late 1978, provoking the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uganda-tanzania-war">Uganda–Tanzania War</a>, in which Tanzanian forces drove out the invaders and went on to capture <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kampala">Kampala</a> in April 1979, ending Amin's rule.</p></div>
